      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} oh, 2 more things in this case:\n\ni suppose you're doing this because some of those changes would break interactions between users and such. i'm wondering, if those cases could be split between:\n\n1. the current situation: instance gets reset, every gets ejected and rejoined\n\n2. instance gets closed, but users who are already there are using the same old networking so they're fine to stay there for up to another day or so.\n\n3. possibly special case of #2 when there's only 1 user in that instance, who can't interact with anyone in the first place. everything on that instance could become effectively local/not-networked\n\nand also it would be appreciated to change the received fake message to something more appropriate like \"we apologize, but we gotta boot you. xoxo\".",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
